[216.0305, "o", "\r\nKernel saw promotion request:\r\nCandidate: runtime/releases/v001-candidate\r\nReason: Add a 'browser' tool (Playwright headless Chromium) that navigates to a URL and returns the page title + a visible-text snippet, for pages needing JS rendering that fetch_url can't handle. Protected by new ratchet check check_browser_tool_registered_and_guarded (tool is canonical, wired into _HANDLERS, rejects non-http(s) URLs). Verified live against https://example.com through the runtime dispatch. System deps persisted to state/system-deps.txt so Chromium's shared libs survive FREE-sandbox restarts; playwright pip pkg + chromium browser installed into persistent HOME cache. Also fixed a pre-existing FREE-sandbox gap where check_prompt_warns_about_missing_optional_binaries failed because _ENV_FREE lacked the missing-optional-binary guidance present in _ENV_SAFE.\r\n"]
[216.0335, "o", "\r\nKernel gate for: runtime/releases/v001-candidate\r\n"]
[216.1488, "o", "$ /usr/local/bin/python /eva/runtime/releases/v001-candidate/tests.py --self\r\n"]
[216.3988, "o", "  ok · all checks passed.\r\n$ /usr/local/bin/python /eva/runtime/releases/v001-candidate/supervisor.py --smoke\r\n"]
[216.6488, "o", "  ok · supervisor smoke ok\r\n"]
[216.6489, "o", "$ /usr/local/bin/python /eva/runtime/releases/v001-candidate/supervisor.py --qualification-round kernel-1\r\n"]
[216.8989, "o", "  ok · qualification round kernel-1 ok\r\n"]
[216.899, "o", "$ /usr/local/bin/python /eva/runtime/releases/v001-candidate/supervisor.py --qualification-round kernel-2\r\n"]
[217.149, "o", "  ok · qualification round kernel-2 ok\r\n"]
[217.1491, "o", "Promote candidate after kernel gate? [y/N] "]
[217.3991, "o", "y"]
